---
description: Save durable, verified knowledge in the local Markdown library
argument-hint: "<fact, decision, or lesson>"
---
Record the following information in the private Markdown knowledge library under
`~/.pi/memory/`:

$ARGUMENTS

Load the `persistent-memory` skill and follow its scope, safety, indexing, locking,
and Jujutsu transaction requirements. Read relevant indexes and existing notes
before writing. If no information was provided, ask what should be remembered.

Save only durable, confirmed, non-sensitive project or topic knowledge. Update an
existing note instead of adding a duplicate. If the request is a user preference
or workflow instruction, explain that it belongs in `~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md`, a
project `AGENTS.md`, or a specialized skill rather than the knowledge library.

If the information is ambiguous, sensitive, unverified, or too ephemeral, explain
why and ask for clarification rather than storing it. Finish by stating exactly
what was saved and which note changed.
